validate\\n  the diagnostic run instead of silently dropping samples or blocking inference.\\n- Legacy aggregates and detailed capture reuse timestamp and interval reads.\\n\\n## Tests and actual flows\\n\\n18 tests passed; one opt-in full GPU feature matrix skipped. This includes the\\nrepository's lightweight feature-matrix contract test, affected KV-metrics tests,\\nand regression coverage for direct readiness, event reuse, clock separation,\\nmodel/logits scopes, cached clipping, shutdown drain and output backpressure.\\nSyntax/diff checks passed. Standards and requirements were reviewed directly.\\n\\nReal GH200/70B offline driver, CD3 fused + compressed KV, batch 16, input length\\n1020, generation 33, dedicated KV blocks 16, planner blocks 4096, first 4 decode\\nintervals excluded for the comparison. Same driver/options and fresh processes:\\n\\n| Warmed decode metric | Original breakdown | Corrected breakdown |\\n|---|---:|---:|\\n| TPOT mean | 132.95 ms | 138.30 ms |\\n| GPU model-forward mean | 93.1979 ms | 94.5436 ms |\\n\\nObserved differences: TPOT +4.02%, model-forward +1.44%. These are one paired\\ncomparison, not universal overhead bounds or an uninstrumented comparison.\\nThe previously delivered implementation had shown TPOT +18.97% in the earlier\\naudit. Added capture cost in the corrected run averaged about 2.73 ms/forward;\\nMessagePack enqueue cost about 0.32 ms/forward. The latter is measured outside\\nGPUFwd; neither metric includes all pre-existing breakdown costs.\\n\\nOffline recorded 34 complete model partitions and 34 separate logits intervals;\\nall 13,600 host prefetch observations were preserved. 13,598 waits had direct\\nreadiness timestamps; two prefill events re-recorded after their wait were NA.\\nModel state/region sums agreed with model-forward durations.\\n\\nReal serving suite `--smoke --breakdown`, CD3 kvcomp, chunk 8192, max-num-seqs 2,\\ndedicated KV blocks 16: two HTTP requests completed and the server shut down\\nnormally. The suite automatically converted and summarized snapshots. There were\\n127 complete model+logits forwards, 5,840 KV H2D windows covering 80 layers, and\\n50,800 host prefetch observations. Three re-recorded ready events were NA; all\\nother wait rows used direct events. Producer and worker both reported 127 frames,\\nzero drops, no errors. Exact-state sums agreed with GPUFwd. GPU/hugepage resources\\nreturned to idle and no output worker remained alive.\\n\\n## Limits\\n\\nThese are instrumented event-window measurements, not pure DMA/SM busy time or\\nzero-interference observations. Device event resolution and enabled readiness\\ntimestamps still have cost. No exact CPU-enqueue-to-GPU-start latency is claimed:\\nhost and GPU timestamps have separate clock origins. Lateness is the observed\\nlocal dependency, not a counterfactual total-stall attribution.\\n\\nThe direct offline driver writes snapshots; its documented post-run summary\\ncommand was used to export the CSVs. Serving was verified through the full suite\\nentry point, including automatic export and normal multiprocessing finalization.\\nEOF\\nls -lh /home/ubuntu/tiered-breakdown-evidence/corrected/VERIFICATION.md /home/ubuntu/tiered-breakdown-evidence/corrected/interval-breakdown.patch\",\"max_output_tokens\":1000}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0aa87-f474-7e62-9f22-c53c13193a25","create_time":1789569245.125579}}}
